  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ashok vs Union Of India And 4 Others on 4 July, 2024 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc:108504-Db Court No . - 40 Case :- Writ - C No. - 16993 of 2024 Petitioner :- Ashok Respondent :- Union Of India And 4 Others Counsel for Petitioner :- A.K.Srivastava,Gopal Srivastava Counsel for Respondent :- A.S.G.I. with Case :- Writ - C No. - 42028 of 2023 Petitioner :- Ashok Respondent :- Union Of India And 3 Others Counsel for Petitioner :- A.K.Srivastava,Gopal Srivastava Counsel for Respondent :- A.S.G.I.,Krishna Agarawal Hon'ble Shekhar B. Saraf,J. Hon'ble Manjive Shukla,J. 1.",
    "facts": "In earlier round of litigation, a co-ordinate Bench of this Court by order dated December 6, 2023 permitted the petitioner to continue with his retail snacks and tea shop on the Railway Platform provided he deposits the requisite commission as indicated in his licence. Upon expiry of the period of the said certificate, the impugned orders were passed by the respondents authorities wherein the petitioner was denied the right to continue with his retail snacks and tea shop on the Railway Platform. The reason provided in the impugned orders is dual in nature - firstly, it was stated that petitioner did not have the proper FSSAI certificate and secondly, it was stated that petitioner had attained the age of 60 years and therefore, could not continue as a Commission Vendor. 4.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner has submitted that the ground taken in the impugned orders with regard to the age of the petitioner is completely arbitrary and is required to be rejected outright as the petitioner is not a Government employee and no age restriction applies to him. However, learned counsel appearing for the petitioner could not explain the reason for not having a valid FSSAI certificate."
  },
